    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">This is <strong>Chapter 3</strong> of the <strong>Digital Logic Basics</strong> series.<br><br>In this chapter, you will simulate binary addition using logic gates.<br><br>A binary adder takes two bits and produces:<br>- a sum bit<br>- a carry bit<br><br>You will evaluate a multi-bit addition using chained adders.<br><br>Each bit position uses a FULL ADDER, defined as:<br><br>sum = A XOR B XOR Cin<br>carry = (A AND B) OR (Cin AND (A XOR B))<br><br>Where:<br>- A and B are the input bits<br>- Cin is the carry-in from the previous position<br><br>The least significant bit (rightmost) has Cin = 0.<br><br>Given two binary numbers of equal length, you must compute:<br>- the final binary sum<br>- including the final carry (if any)</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> A string <var>A</var> &mdash; binary number<br><strong>Line 2:</strong> A string <var>B</var> &mdash; binary number<br><br>Both strings have the same length and consist of <const>0</const> and <const>1</const> only.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> A binary string &mdash; the sum of <var>A</var> and <var>B</var> (including final carry if present)</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">1 &le; length of <var>A</var> &le; 32<br><var>A</var>, <var>B</var> contain only <const>0</const>, <const>1</const></div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">0\n0</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">0</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
